      "scope": "Finite one-mutex, one terminating thread, one contender, one queued waiter, two processors as the collective. initEither retains the thread ticket and clears end-condvar while that ticket is held, with inverse locker entry and slow path, inverse unlock, owner/queue recheck, marker admission, and abandon participation. Alias 0/1/2 and locker versus unlocker are free. Negative initializers are incomplete repairs. The state machine does not include the thread-group lock, the signal new-owner acquire, or waiter/new-owner address order. This is not source refinement, not a native admission, and not a cause of the retained TFIB or pipe timeout."
