      "scope": "Finite two-role ticket and collective protocol, one queue publication, no unbounded arrivals. The holder entering a collective is a conditional premise, not the retained native owner or sop.op identification. The positive initializer is the Scheme failed-trylock path in ##thread-intr-propagate!: participate without an outstanding ticket, recheck target membership, publish the relocated payload, release, then notify that processor id. A non-member is scheduled locally and does not publish. The exported C ___raise_high_level_interrupt_pstate still reserves if called and is not this positive run. Served-ticket polling is not the source repair. Initially valid negative controls reach raw-wait deadlock, stale payload publication, repeated-reservation orphaning, early notification and publication onto a non-member. Weak fairness covers only this finite operation. No C/ARM memory-order refinement, full GC/resize lifecycle proof, identification of the retained holder, or native admission."
